2	 * VelaPaw - OV5640 camera backend (real hardware, ESP32-S3 LCD_CAM/DVP)
3	 *
4	 * The board driver (esp32s3_st7789.c) owns the OV5640 + LCD_CAM + GDMA and
5	 * captures a QVGA (320x240) RGB565 frame on demand. This HAL downscales that
6	 * to the model/UI's 128x128 RGB888, applies the SELFIE mirror (the lens faces
7	 * the back of the board, so we flip horizontally to act like a front camera),
8	 * and returns it. Flat build: we call the board capture function directly.
9	 *
10	 * The raw DVP capture comes out of the sensor/mount rotated 90 deg CCW from
11	 * the real scene (confirmed on hardware: a hand held upright renders sideways)
12	 * -- flip/mirror registers (0x3820/0x3821) can never fix this, since they only
13	 * reverse an axis and a 90 deg turn needs an actual transpose. We correct it
14	 * here in the resample step with a 90 deg CW remap, combined with the selfie
15	 * mirror on the final (post-rotation) horizontal axis.
16	 ****************************************************************************/
